# Dict patterns use open matching by default: extra keys in the scrutinee are ignored.
# A pattern [ok: v] matches any dict that has an "ok" key, regardless of other keys present.
# This test verifies that extra keys ("extra") do NOT prevent a match.
[match [ok: 42  extra: "data"]
  [case [let v] [ok: v] v]
  ...:          99]
=== out
Int(42)
